BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a sacred river. The river had a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        peculiar blessing: any gift cast into its waters from the upstream village would emerge ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        threefold at the downstream village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      The Upstream dwellers received five coins each moon from the celestial spirits. They could) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (         choose to cast some into the river, knowing the water would triple it for their Downstr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        eam neighbors. The Downstream people, upon receiving this abundance, could return gifts ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        upstream-though the current made this journey harder, with no multiplication.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      A wise elder taught: "True prosperity flows like the river itself. When Upstream shares ge) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        nerously, Downstream flourishes and can return gratitude. Both villages grow rich togeth) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        er. But when fear or greed stops the flow, both banks grow barren.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      Some moons, mist clouded the waters, and gifts appeared larger or smaller than they truly ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        were. The villages learned that trust must persist even when vision fails.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The greatest prosperity came when Upstream gave freely, trusting in return, and when Downs) Tj ET
