BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        Rain faced a choice: hoard the droplets or release them to the River below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      When the Rain let the droplets fall, a miracle occurred-each droplet multiplied threefold ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        as it descended. The River swelled with fifteen silver drops, suddenly abundant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      But the River, too, faced a choice. It could keep all fifteen drops, leaving the Rain depl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        eted forever. Or it could send some back, returning the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The wise River understood: the Rain had made itself vulnerable by giving first. The Rain h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ad created abundance where scarcity lived. So the River sent back seven drops, keeping e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        ight.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      The Rain now held seven instead of five. The River held eight instead of zero.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      And so the cycle continued, round after round, each participant sometimes giving, sometime) Tj ET
